# ============================================================================
# PengyOS Desktop — amdgpu runtime-PM / d3cold udev rule
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part of the Desktop board rootfs-overlay
# (etc/udev/rules.d/). Drives the amdgpu DRM device to the deepest idle power
# well (d3cold) when the integrated GPU is idle, which is the dominant power
# win on a hybrid AMD-iGPU + NVIDIA-dGPU laptop.
#
# NVIDIA vendor wiring is OUT of scope (SPEC §2.4–2.5): this rule only touches the
# open amdgpu DRM device (the iGPU that owns the eDP panel).
# ============================================================================

# amdgpu DRM card. Idle -> d3cold. The card node itself has no driver
# (DRIVER==""), so match the PCI parent with DRIVERS; the runtime-PM knobs are
# the parent's power/ attributes (there is no runtime_power/), and udev values
# must be quoted. Before 26.10.22 all three were wrong: udev rejected the rule
# ("Invalid key/value pair", behoweather 26.10.20) and the change rule below
# never matched.
# autosuspend_delay_ms arms the autosuspend timer (idle before trip).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", DRIVERS=="amdgpu", \
  ATTR{device/power/autosuspend_delay_ms}="2000", \
  ATTR{device/power/control}="auto"

# Re-arm the timer whenever the amdgpu device is re-activated (e.g. after a
# PRIME offload round-trip) so it trips d3cold again once idle.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", DRIVERS=="amdgpu", \
  ATTR{device/power/control}="auto"
